# No handoff-as-architecture

## Allowed in `*_HANDOFF*.md` / `DEVELOPER_HANDOFF.md`

- Local run steps, ports, smoke checklists
- Temporary local-only notes
- “What we shipped today” narrative

## Not allowed as the source of truth

- Counting rules, SSOT, identity keys, window/contiguous rules
- “Dual engines / dual clients OK as non-blocking follow-up”
- API contracts the backend must obey

Those belong in `.cursor/rules/`, `docs/adr/`, and domain modules (`reportMenuDefs`, shared form sections, projection utils).

If a handoff documents a correctness debt, either **fix it in the same ship** or escalate it to a blocking checklist item — do not ship “ready” with dual clients or wrong windows.
